  "goodToKnow": "Das Gesundheitsamt is the local public health office, run by districts and cities. It handles infectious disease reporting, school health checks, hygiene inspections and vaccination advice. During the COVID-19 pandemic, Gesundheitsämter became famous for contact tracing, often still using fax. At federal level, the Robert Koch-Institut in Berlin monitors public health. Plural: die Gesundheitsämter."
